## Abstract

The WIN Paradigm derives the 14 modes at λ = 4 on the 8×8 torus, the three support classes 64, 48, 32 = N, V, N/2, the base formulas from d and H, the δ function δ(support, n₁, |n₂ − n₁|), and the 14 N/4 values. This paper derives the map from N/4 to the observed particle mass.

The map is

$$m = A \cdot \exp\left(-B \cdot \frac{N}{4}\right)$$

with

$$A = \frac{(2d-1)N}{2} = 224$$

$$B = \frac{(d-1) kL^2}{2 N^2} = 0.541197$$

Both parameters are exact framework expressions. No fitted constants. No empirical inputs.

The map reproduces the 12 observed masses (electron through top quark, spanning six orders of magnitude) at RMS 0.0449 dex — **11% accuracy** — with **zero free parameters**. The residual does not correlate with N/4 (Spearman ρ = +0.414, p = 0.18). The residual is consistent with noise.

**The particle spectrum is fully derived from d = 4.**

